WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.840
Has the Marvel Cinematic Universe finally
found its Adam Warlock?

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.700
Entertainment news site We Got This Covered
claims they have an anonymous source with

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:12.099
insider knowledge, and that source says Marvel
Studios executives are eyeing Stranger Things

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.720
breakout star Dacre Montgomery to portray
Adam Warlock in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.220
3.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:21.820
This undisclosed source also says Montgomery
is actually one of many actors that the studio

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.950
has placed on its Warlock wishlist, so hardcore
fans of his shouldn't go screaming on social

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.780
media that he's a shoo-in for the part.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.660
The insider also stated that casting for Guardians
of the Galaxy Vol. 3 hasn't even officially

00:00:32.669 --> 00:00:37.271
begun as of mid-July 2019, though they did
share that Montgomery is likely to be "in

00:00:37.271 --> 00:00:41.910
the running" once Marvel and writer-director
James Gunn finally get the gears on the long-awaited

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.940
threequel turning.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:47.440
Third-party reports claim that casting for
the third Guardians movie will begin in November,

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.250
so it seems plausible that Marvel could start
making a list of contenders a few months in

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:51.740
advance.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.780
It should be noted that Marvel hasn't actually
confirmed the presence of Adam Warlock in

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.480
Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3, so we're not
entirely sure if the character will even be

00:00:59.480 --> 00:00:59.980
a part of the story.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.720
Talk amongst the Marvel community claims that
Adam, the artificially created being meant

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.820
to serve as the perfect human and the pinnacle
of evolution, will somehow cross paths with

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:12.950
the Guardians as they search for their lost
member Gamora after the past version of herself

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:15.560
vanished during the battle with Thanos in
Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:19.220
The reason for this theory is down to two
things: a mid-credits scene from Guardians

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.060
of the Galaxy Vol. 2, in which the Sovereign
High Priestess Ayesha reveals that she created

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.080
a powerful being to destroy the Guardians:

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.100
"I think I shall call him, 'Adam'."

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:35.140
And then there's Gunn's past mention that
Adam was meant to appear in Guardians Vol.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:38.260
2, but would instead pop up in a later franchise
installment.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.820
In 2017, Gunn discouraged fans from believing
that Adam would definitely be in Guardians

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:47.119
Vol. 3, though that clearly hasn't stopped
them from speculating about the exact opposite.

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:51.939
Adam Warlock's MCU debut feels inevitable,
and it's certainly a long time coming, given

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:56.200
that he was even in talks to appear in the
supersized superhero ensemble Avengers: Endgame.

00:01:56.329 --> 00:02:00.060
Such an appearance would have been appropriate,
since Adam has had a complicated history with

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:04.479
Endgame's main antagonist Thanos, first partnering
with the Mad Titan to destroy his eventual

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.900
evil alter ego Magus, then serving as his
biggest rival.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.400
Endgame screenwriters Christopher Markus and
Stephen McFeely ultimately felt like it would

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.900
be too much of a, quote, "backbend" to introduce
Adam in the film, so that seedling of a thought

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:17.800
never sprouted.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:22.760
Montgomery would be a nice fit for Adam Warlock,
as the 24-year-old Aussie actor has had experience

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:27.650
in the superhero arena before, previously
playing the Red Ranger in 2017's Power Rangers

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.140
reboot.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:32.040
He may face fierce competition in the fight
to portray Adam Warlock - if he's truly in

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.519
consideration for it, of course.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:38.269
Zac Efron, who recently stunned in Netflix's
Extremely Wicked, Shockingly Evil and Vile,

00:02:38.269 --> 00:02:41.420
has also been rumored to be up for the role
in Guardians Vol. 3.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:45.560
Even if Montgomery does lose out on the gig,
the Stranger Things star could very well be

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:48.660
a part of the superhero franchise in a totally
different capacity.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:53.040
Many fans are hoping that once Marvel Studios
reboots the X-Men franchise in the aftermath

00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:57.739
of Disney's acquisition of 20th Century Fox,
Montgomery will become the new Wolverine - a

00:02:57.739 --> 00:03:01.599
younger version of the character famously
played by fellow Aussie Hugh Jackman.

00:03:01.599 --> 00:03:05.730
At this stage, it's all just speculation,
but one thing is clear: Dacre Montgomery is

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:07.020
having one hell of a summer.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:08.280
"Perfect form."

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.860
"Well, your form is amazing."

